From: The Surface Duo port <none@invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 18/18] overview: no thumbnail for an activity nobody can see

The overview asks the compositor for a thumbnail of a window whenever the
window changes, so that its activity is ready when the overview is opened.
On a display with a seam the overview is never shown - the home surface is
hidden there (patch 0016) - and the thumbnails were taken all the same: 53
in 20 launches from the dock, each a 675x898 window read back from the GPU,
in the middle of the launch. Now and then one of them was a buffer the
compositor would not take ("Unsupported format", wl_shm.invalid_format),
and it disconnected the shell, which restarted the whole session.

A thumbnail is asked for only when the activity can be seen. An activity
shown again asks again: phosh_overview_refresh, or its window's next
change. On a phone without a seam the home is always there and nothing
changes.
---
--- a/src/overview.c
+++ b/src/overview.c
@@ -251,6 +251,19 @@
   int scale;
   g_return_if_fail (PHOSH_IS_ACTIVITY (activity));
   g_return_if_fail (PHOSH_IS_TOPLEVEL (toplevel));
+
+  /*
+   * A thumbnail nobody can see is a window read back from the GPU for
+   * nothing. The overview asks for one whenever a window changes, and on a
+   * display with a seam it is never shown (the home surface is hidden,
+   * patch 0016): 53 thumbnails in 20 launches, in the middle of each. One
+   * of them, now and then, was a buffer phoc would not take, and phoc
+   * disconnected the shell (#196). An activity that can be seen again
+   * asks again - phosh_overview_refresh, or the window's next change.
+   */
+  if (!gtk_widget_is_visible (GTK_WIDGET (activity)))
+    return;
+
   scale = gtk_widget_get_scale_factor (GTK_WIDGET (activity));
   phosh_activity_get_thumbnail_allocation (activity, &allocation);
   thumbnail = phosh_toplevel_thumbnail_new_from_toplevel (toplevel, allocation.width * scale, allocation.height * scale);
